# .gitignore for a Black Ops III mod-tools root (the install folder itself).
#
# Why track the install, not just usermaps/<map>: overriding stock content means
# editing shared files (zone_source/all/assetlist/*.csv, GDTs, deffiles) that
# affect every map built from this tree; community packs install straight into
# source_data/, model_export/, deffiles/; Steam "verify files" and APE saves
# overwrite files silently. A commit per change makes all of it reviewable and
# revertible, and lets an agent read what changed since the last good build.
#
# What this keeps out: what the tools regenerate, and large binary art. The art
# formats below are ignored so that `git add .` never sweeps in gigabytes of
# stock textures and sounds. To version your OWN source art or exports, add them
# explicitly with `git add -f <path>`; the companion .gitattributes stores the
# binary ones in Git LFS (run `git lfs install` once).
#
# First commit: the install is ~10 GB. Commit in steps, starting with what you
# edit: zone_source/all/assetlist/, deffiles/, source_data/, share/raw/,
# usermaps/, mods/; then the rest.

# Generated by the tools
share/assetconvert/
LPC/.manifest
steam_appid.txt
steam_autocloud.vdf
radiant/autosave_backup/
*.bak
*.tmp
*.cache
*.dmp
*.stackdump

# Executables and binaries
*.exe
*.dll
*.bin
*.obj
*.pri
*.pyc

# Build output (link, compile, light)
*.ff
*.xpak
*.d3dbsp
*.gdb
*.cgp
*.hkt
*.lin
*.led
*.sabl
*.sabs
usermaps/*/zone/snd/
usermaps/*/zone_source/*/
usermaps/**/sound/zone/*
mods/*/zone/snd/
mods/*/zone_source/*/

# Databases (gdtdb/gdt.db, t7kb.db…)
*.db
*.db-shm
*.db-wal

# Large binary art and exports: ignored; `git add -f` your own (see the header)
*.tif
*.tiff
*.tga
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.gif
*.dds
*.exr
*.hdr
*.psd
*.xcf
*.wav
*.mkv
# .efx is text: share/raw/fx holds ~10k stock effects (~500 MB); `git add -f` yours
# (they stay plain git, so their diffs read)
*.efx
*.semodel
*.cast
*.mel
*.mtl
*.fd
*.icn
*.lvi
*.siege_anim_source
*.xmodel_bin
*.XMODEL_BIN
*.xmodel_export
*.XMODEL_EXPORT
*.xanim_bin
*.XANIM_BIN
*.xanim_export
*.xcam_export

# Logs
*.log
*.errlog
*.gltn

# Extraction tools' working folders (their .cfg/.ini included)
.extract_assets/
_extract_assets/
*.tscproj

# Optional: the boiii client (theater mode in custom maps) — uncomment if you use it
# boiii_players/
# data/
# cache
# workshop_cache.json

# Optional: bo3tool (camera, fog and lighting in theater mode)
# .bo3tool/
